        "root_concepts": "[voice, leading]",
        "section": "music-theory",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Voice Leading and Counterpoint",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The search space is enormous (each voice has ~20 feasible pitches × 4 voices × N time steps), but the constraints propagate aggressively. This is why DeepBach (Hadjeres et al., 2017) models SATB harmonization as probabilistic inference: given constraints, sample from the posterior distribution over valid voice assignments."
    },
    {
      "id": "05-VOICE-LEADING-COUNTERPOINT.md#014",
      "path": [
        "05-VOICE-LEADING-COUNTERPOINT.md"
