        "root_concepts": "[voice, leading]",
        "section": "music-theory",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Voice Leading and Counterpoint",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nFOUR TYPES OF MOTION BETWEEN TWO VOICES:\n  Parallel: both voices move in the same direction by the same interval type\n  Similar:  both voices move in the same direction by different intervals\n  Contrary: voices move in opposite directions (preferred)\n  Oblique:  one voice holds, other moves"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-VOICE-LEADING-COUNTERPOINT.md#016",
      "path": [
        "05-VOICE-LEADING-COUNTERPOINT.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:music-theory:05-voice-leading-counterpoint, git-history:music-theory:05-voice-leading-counterpoint]",
        "canonical_path": "music-theory/05-VOICE-LEADING-COUNTERPOINT.md",
        "concepts": "[voice, leading, counterpoint]",
        "current_path": "music-theory/05-VOICE-LEADING-COUNTERPOINT.md",
        "id": "maxim:music-theory:voice-leading-counterpoint",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "music-theory",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[voice, leading]",
        "section": "music-theory",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Voice Leading and Counterpoint",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "FORBIDDEN MOTIONS:\n  1. Parallel fifths (P5→P5): two voices maintaining a fifth apart while both move\n     C–G to D–A: FORBIDDEN\n     Why: two voices \"fuse\" into one timbre — voice independence lost\n          Historically heard as medieval, regression to organum"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-VOICE-LEADING-COUNTERPOINT.md#017",
      "path": [
        "05-VOICE-LEADING-COUNTERPOINT.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:music-theory:05-voice-leading-counterpoint, git-history:music-theory:05-voice-leading-counterpoint]",
        "canonical_path": "music-theory/05-VOICE-LEADING-COUNTERPOINT.md",
        "concepts": "[voice, leading, counterpoint]",
        "current_path": "music-theory/05-VOICE-LEADING-COUNTERPOINT.md",
        "id": "maxim:music-theory:voice-leading-counterpoint",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "music-theory",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[voice, leading]",
        "section": "music-theory",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Voice Leading and Counterpoint",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "2. Parallel octaves (P8→P8): same pitch doubling at octave while both move\n     C–C to D–D: FORBIDDEN\n     Why: voices become identical, lose identity as separate lines"
    },
    {
