      "text": "```\nLEADING TONE RULE: The leading tone (scale degree 7) must resolve up to tonic\n  In V or V7 → I, the 7th degree MUST go to the tonic\n  Exception: leading tone in inner voice (A or T) may occasionally go down\n             to the 5th of I if needed to complete the chord"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-VOICE-LEADING-COUNTERPOINT.md#021",
      "path": [
        "05-VOICE-LEADING-COUNTERPOINT.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:music-theory:05-voice-leading-counterpoint, git-history:music-theory:05-voice-leading-counterpoint]",
        "canonical_path": "music-theory/05-VOICE-LEADING-COUNTERPOINT.md",
        "concepts": "[voice, leading, counterpoint]",
        "current_path": "music-theory/05-VOICE-LEADING-COUNTERPOINT.md",
        "id": "maxim:music-theory:voice-leading-counterpoint",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "music-theory",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[voice, leading]",
        "section": "music-theory",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Voice Leading and Counterpoint",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "V7 → I resolution in C major:\n    G7 (G B D F) → C (C E G)\n    G: stays as G (common tone rule — common tones held)\n    B: resolves UP to C (leading tone → tonic) ↑\n    D: resolves DOWN to C or up to E (choose based on voice)\n    F: resolves DOWN to E (7th of chord resolves down by step) ↓"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-VOICE-LEADING-COUNTERPOINT.md#022",
      "path": [
        "05-VOICE-LEADING-COUNTERPOINT.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:music-theory:05-voice-leading-counterpoint, git-history:music-theory:05-voice-leading-counterpoint]",
        "canonical_path": "music-theory/05-VOICE-LEADING-COUNTERPOINT.md",
        "concepts": "[voice, leading, counterpoint]",
        "current_path": "music-theory/05-VOICE-LEADING-COUNTERPOINT.md",
        "id": "maxim:music-theory:voice-leading-counterpoint",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
