        "root_concepts": "[voice, leading]",
        "section": "music-theory",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Voice Leading and Counterpoint",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "DOUBLED NOTES:\n  Root position: double the root (preferred), or the fifth\n  NEVER double the leading tone (already has strong tendency — doubling\n    would require parallel octaves or awkward resolution)\n  First inversion: double the soprano note or root (avoid doubling the bass = 3rd)\n  Second inversion (I⁶₄): double the 5th (which is in the bass)\n```"
    },
