        "root_concepts": "[voice, leading]",
        "section": "music-theory",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Voice Leading and Counterpoint",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nAUTHENTIC CADENCE (AC): V(7) → I\n  Perfect Authentic (PAC): V → I, both in ROOT POSITION, soprano ends on tonic (1̂)\n    Strongest possible ending — full stop, resolved\n  Imperfect Authentic (IAC): V → I but:\n    - V or I not in root position (inversion used), OR\n    - Soprano does not land on scale degree 1\n    Weaker, sense of continuation"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-VOICE-LEADING-COUNTERPOINT.md#028",
      "path": [
        "05-VOICE-LEADING-COUNTERPOINT.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:music-theory:05-voice-leading-counterpoint, git-history:music-theory:05-voice-leading-counterpoint]",
        "canonical_path": "music-theory/05-VOICE-LEADING-COUNTERPOINT.md",
        "concepts": "[voice, leading, counterpoint]",
        "current_path": "music-theory/05-VOICE-LEADING-COUNTERPOINT.md",
        "id": "maxim:music-theory:voice-leading-counterpoint",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "music-theory",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[voice, leading]",
        "section": "music-theory",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Voice Leading and Counterpoint",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "HALF CADENCE (HC): ends on V (no resolution)\n  Any chord → V\n  Feels like a question — \"comma\" in the phrase, not a full stop\n  Common endings: I → V, ii → V, IV → V, ii⁶ → V"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-VOICE-LEADING-COUNTERPOINT.md#029",
      "path": [
        "05-VOICE-LEADING-COUNTERPOINT.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:music-theory:05-voice-leading-counterpoint, git-history:music-theory:05-voice-leading-counterpoint]",
        "canonical_path": "music-theory/05-VOICE-LEADING-COUNTERPOINT.md",
        "concepts": "[voice, leading, counterpoint]",
        "current_path": "music-theory/05-VOICE-LEADING-COUNTERPOINT.md",
        "id": "maxim:music-theory:voice-leading-counterpoint",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "music-theory",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[voice, leading]",
        "section": "music-theory",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Voice Leading and Counterpoint",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "PLAGAL CADENCE (PC): IV → I\n  \"Church\" cadence (the \"Amen\" cadence)\n  Softer, less directed than authentic — more conclusive than half\n  Can follow an authentic cadence to extend the ending"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-VOICE-LEADING-COUNTERPOINT.md#030",
